# UI & Modern Component Rules

## 1. UI Library Standard
- Use `shadcn-svelte` (built on top of `bits-ui`) for all UI interactions (Dialogs, Sheets, Dropdowns, Tabs, Tooltips).
- NEVER build raw HTML inputs, dropdowns, or modals if a `shadcn-svelte` component exists for it.
- If a component is missing, ask the user to run `npx shadcn-svelte@latest add <component-name>`.

## 2. Micro-interactions & Animations
- Use `lucide-svelte` exclusively for standard UI icons.
- Apply smooth CSS transitions using Tailwind classes (e.g., `transition-all duration-200 ease-in-out`).
- Ensure all forms, buttons, and interactive cards have explicit visual hover, active, and focus states.
